/bja.ojp.gov/sites/g/files/xyckuh186/files/media/document/reengineeringtrainin \ng1.pdf \nPolice Executive Research Forum (PERF). (2021). What police chiefs and sheriffs need to know \nabout collecting and analyzing use-of-force data. \nhttps://www.policeforum.org/assets/CollectingAnalyzingUOFData.pdf \nPolice1. (2022, October 6). N.Y. city reaches $12M settlement for family of Daniel Prude. \nhttps://www.police1.com/use-of-force/articles/ny-city-reaches-12m-settlement-for- \nfamily-of-daniel-prude-Rdn58dEEnYBUhkif/ \nPresident’s Task Force on 21st Century Policing. (2015). Final report of the President’s Task \nForce on 21st Century Policing. Office of Community Oriented Policing Services. \nPrior, R. (2021, June 10). Use of neck restraints by law enforcement should be prohibited, \nAmerican Academy of Neurology Says. CNN. \nhttps://www.cnn.com/2021/06/10/health/american-academy-of-neurology-neck- \nrestraints/index.html \nRabe-Hemp, C. E. (2008). Female officers and the ethic of care: Does officer gender impact \npolice behaviors? Journal of Criminal Justice, 36(5), 426–434.\n\nNIJ DCRA Study: Environmental Scan of Context and Policies Related to Arrest-Related Deaths \nJune 2024 Final Page 87 \n \n \n \nRichardson, B. C., Rengifo, J., Stanton, M., Nevarez, N., Roman, C., Ranucci, A., Harley, A., \nMason, S., & Judd, T. (2021). Cerebrovascular and pathological findings in police \nchokehold fatalities [International Stroke Conference 2021 Poster Abstract P639]. \nStroke, 52(Suppl. 1). https://doi.org/10.1161/str.52.suppl_1.P639 \nRidgeway, G. (2016). Officer risk factors associated with police shootings: A matched case- \ncontrol study. Statistics and Public Policy, 3(1), 1–6. \nRoach, B., Echols, K., & Burnett, A. (2014, July). Excited delirium and the dual response: \nPreventing in-custody deaths (NCJ No. 248101). https://www.ojp.gov/ncjrs/virtual- \nlibrary/abstracts/excited-delirium-and-dual-response-preventing-custody-deaths-0 \nRosenbaum, D. P., & Lawrence, 